    "Sentiment history (especially negative spikes like -1.0) does not trigger downward corrections in the forecast, leading to systematic overshoots when sentiment turns bearish.",
    "Model ignores immediate volatility clustering; after a high price spike in history, it continues to predict higher prices instead of anticipating a correction phase.",
    "Bias increases as the forecast horizon extends beyond 14 days, where true outcomes consistently revert toward historical averages rather than following the model's trend."
